+# 01: Reserve and look up a Reservation (full holds)
+
+**What to build:** The cart service can reserve stock for a cart in a warehouse and look the Reservation up again. This is the tracer bullet. In this ticket every requested line is fully Available (partial holds come in 02). While the Reservation is active, its units are Held: they no longer count as Available, so neither another Reservation nor `place_order` can take them. Allocated is unchanged. See the spec at `.scratch/stock-reservations/spec.md` and the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `ReservationStatus` (ACTIVE, CONFIRMED, RELEASED, EXPIRED) and `Reservation` exist with the fields named in the spec (`reservation_id`, `warehouse`, `items`, `status`, `expires_at`, `order_id`, then `requested`, `reserved_at`), and both are exported from the package
+- [x] `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` exist as `InventoryError` subclasses carrying the context attributes the spec lists
+- [x] `reserve(warehouse, items, idempotency_key)` with fully Available stock returns an ACTIVE Reservation: `items` equal to the request, `requested` equal to the request, `order_id` None, `reserved_at` = clock now, `expires_at` = now + 20 minutes
+- [x] The service accepts an optional `reservation_ttl` keyword (default 20 minutes), and `expires_at` follows it; construction with only repository, ledger and clock still works
+- [x] Reservation ids are sequential: `RES-0001`, `RES-0002`, …
+- [x] Blank idempotency key (empty or whitespace) → `InvalidOrder`; unknown warehouse → `UnknownWarehouse`; empty items → `InvalidOrder`; unknown SKU → `UnknownSku`; zero, negative or non-integer quantity → `InvalidQuantity`. A rejected request holds nothing, not even for its valid lines
+- [x] `get_reservation(id)` returns the Reservation; an unknown id → `ReservationNotFound`
+- [x] New `held(sku, warehouse)` query returns units in active Reservations and validates SKU and warehouse like the other queries
+- [x] `available` = max(0, on-hand − allocated − held); `allocated` is unchanged
+- [x] A Reservation in one warehouse does not change Held or Available in another
+- [x] `place_order` cannot take Held units (raises `InsufficientStock` when only Held units would satisfy it)
+- [x] Tests go in a new reservations test module that uses the existing fixtures and the public service API only; the existing suite passes unchanged
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `stock-reservations` (tip 261fe03); all 91 tests pass.
