+# 02: Partial holds
+
+**What to build:** A Reservation holds what it can rather than failing the whole cart. For each line it holds as many units as are Available right now, up to the Requested quantity. Lines with nothing Available are left out of the held items entirely. The cart service shows the shortfall by comparing held items with `requested`. Reserve fails only when no line can hold anything. `place_order` stays all-or-nothing. See ADR-0001 for why the two differ: do not unify them.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Reserve and look up a Reservation)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Requesting more than is Available holds exactly the Available amount for that line
+- [x] A line with 0 Available is absent from `items` (not present with 0), while the other lines are still held
+- [x] `requested` always records the full original request, including lines left out of `items`
+- [x] Held and Available reflect only the units actually held
+- [x] When no line can hold anything → `InsufficientStock` naming the first requested line (in the caller's order) with its requested quantity and `available=0`; no Reservation is created
+- [x] Validation errors (unknown SKU, bad quantity, …) still reject the whole request even when other lines could be held
+- [x] `place_order` still raises `InsufficientStock` and creates nothing when any line is short
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `stock-reservations` (tip 261fe03); all 91 tests pass.
