+# 04: Release
+
+**What to build:** Checkout can release a Reservation when the customer abandons the cart, returning its units to Available immediately. Release is safe to retry, and releasing a Reservation that already expired is a quiet no-op, so checkout never has to race the expiry time.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Expiry by the clock)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `release_reservation(id)` on an ACTIVE Reservation returns it with status RELEASED; its units are no longer Held and Available recovers immediately
+- [x] Releasing a RELEASED Reservation returns it unchanged (no error)
+- [x] Releasing an EXPIRED Reservation returns it unchanged, still EXPIRED (no error)
+- [x] `get_reservation` on a released Reservation reports RELEASED, also after its expiry time passes
+- [x] Unknown id → `ReservationNotFound`
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `stock-reservations` (tip 261fe03); all 91 tests pass.
