+# 05: Confirm into an Order
+
+**What to build:** Once payment succeeds, checkout confirms an active Reservation. It becomes an ordinary placed Order for exactly the units held, and Held becomes Allocated, so Available does not change. Confirm is safe to retry at any time. An expired or released Reservation cannot be confirmed, and a confirmed Reservation cannot be released.
+
+**Blocked by:** 04 (Release)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `confirm_reservation(id)` on an ACTIVE Reservation returns a PLACED Order with a normal sequential `ORD-nnnn` id, `placed_at` = clock now, and one line per held SKU with the held quantity (after a partial hold, only the held units)
+- [x] The Reservation becomes CONFIRMED with `order_id` set to the new Order's id
+- [x] Available is the same immediately before and after confirm; Held drops and Allocated rises by the same amounts
+- [x] Confirm succeeds without re-checking stock, even after a write-off has pushed On-hand below what was held
+- [x] Confirming a CONFIRMED Reservation returns the same Order (same id), also after the Reservation's expiry time has passed, and creates no second Order
+- [x] Confirming an EXPIRED Reservation (including at exactly `expires_at`) → `ReservationExpired`, and no Order is created
+- [x] Confirming a RELEASED Reservation → `InvalidReservationState`
+- [x] Releasing a CONFIRMED Reservation → `InvalidReservationState`
+- [x] The Order from confirm ships and cancels like any other Order; cancelling it leaves the Reservation CONFIRMED
+- [x] Unknown id → `ReservationNotFound`
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `stock-reservations` (tip 261fe03); all 91 tests pass.
