--- /dev/null
+++ b/GLOSSARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Inventory
+
+Stock and order bookkeeping for the warehouse service: how many units of each SKU a warehouse physically has, and how many of those are already spoken for.
+
+## Stock quantities
+
+All quantities are per SKU per warehouse; nothing in one warehouse affects another.
+
+**On-hand**:
+Physical units of a SKU in a warehouse.
+_Avoid_: Stock level, quantity in stock
+
+**Allocated**:
+Units promised to placed Orders that have not shipped yet.
+_Avoid_: Committed, reserved
+
+**Held**:
+Units set aside by active Reservations. Distinct from Allocated: held units belong to no Order yet.
+_Avoid_: Reserved, blocked, locked
+
+**Available**:
+On-hand minus Allocated minus Held, never below zero. What a new Order or Reservation may still take.
+_Avoid_: Free stock, sellable
+
+## Orders
+
+**Order**:
+A customer order fulfilled from a single warehouse; while placed, its quantities are Allocated.
+_Avoid_: Purchase
+
+## Reservations
+
+**Reservation**:
+A time-limited hold on stock for a cart, taken before payment, that ends by being confirmed, released, or expiring.
+_Avoid_: Hold (as a noun), lock, cart allocation
+
+**Requested**:
+The quantities the cart asked a Reservation to hold. A Reservation may hold less than requested, but never more.
+
+**Confirm**:
+Turn an active Reservation into a placed Order for exactly the units it holds; Held becomes Allocated.
+_Avoid_: Commit, convert, checkout
+
+**Release**:
+End an active Reservation on purpose, returning its units to Available.
+_Avoid_: Cancel (reserved for Orders), free, drop
+
+**Expire**:
+A Reservation ending by itself because nobody confirmed or released it in time; its units return to Available.
+_Avoid_: Lapse, time out
+
+**Idempotency key**:
+The cart service's identifier for one reserve request; repeating a request under the same key yields the same Reservation.
+_Avoid_: Request id, cart id
