@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+# Reservations hold what they can; Orders stay all-or-nothing
+
+A Reservation holds, per line, as many units as are Available at that moment (up to the Requested quantity), drops lines with nothing Available, and fails only when no line can hold anything. `place_order` deliberately stays all-or-nothing. The asymmetry is intentional: at checkout, "only 3 left — we've held them for you" converts better than an error, and the cart service shows the shortfall itself by comparing the Reservation's held items with what it requested. A direct Order is an explicit commitment to exact quantities, so a short Order would be wrong rather than helpful. Do not "fix" the two to behave the same way.
